# What /cleanup deletes in a checkout of this repository, and /mtm after a fully landed worktree.
# One glob per line, relative to the checkout root: `*` stays within a folder, `**` spans folders; name the
# git-ignored folder or file itself. A line starting with `!` keeps what it matches. A trailing `# ...` says how
# it comes back. Never deleted whatever this says: tracked files, .git, .hal/, .secrets/, .env*, plans/, shotfiles/.
# A new unit adds its own build output here (code/<language>/apps/*/dist and the like).

# Build output
code/**/target                                            # cargo build
code/**/dist                                              # the unit's build
code/**/__pycache__                                       # python runs it again
code/**/.pytest_cache                                     # pytest

# Fetched dependencies
code/**/node_modules                                      # the unit's install (bun install)
